    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the `synthesize_ssml.py` file that synthesizes SSML with voice and prosody controls, I need to integrate with a concrete external Text-to-Speech (TTS) provider. Amazon Polly is a suitable choice for this task as it supports SSML and offers various voice and prosody controls. I will import the necessary components from the `boto3` library, which is the AWS SDK for Python, to interact with Amazon Polly. The provider will be identifiable through the import of `boto3` and the use of the `polly` client. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
